# =============================================================================
# CS223-TermProject | .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# Purpose : Keep secrets, generated files, machine-specific configuration,
#           large VM images, and temporary artifacts out of the PUBLIC repo.
# Project : OpenStack 2026.1 / Kolla Ansible / Two-node lab
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   - .gitignore applies only to untracked files. Already-tracked files remain
#     tracked until removed from the Git index/history.
#   - .gitignore is NOT a secret scanner or a security boundary.
#   - Inspect screenshots, terminal output, and text before committing them.
#   - Keep docs/*.md, config/*.example, and evidence/**/*.png under version
#     control after manually checking for confidential information.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 01. Kolla / OpenStack credentials — NEVER commit
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kolla service credentials and generated client credentials.
**/passwords.yml
**/passwords.yaml
**/passwords.yml.*
**/passwords.yaml.*
**/admin-openrc.sh
**/*-openrc.sh
**/openrc.sh
**/clouds.yaml
**/clouds-public.yaml
**/secure.yaml
**/secure.yml

# Credentials used by tools, deployment hosts, or operators.
**/ansible-vault-password*
**/.vault_pass*
**/.config/openstack/
**/.aws/
**/.kube/
**/.ssh/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 02. Original deployment configuration — publish reviewed examples instead
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local/production configuration may include internal endpoints, secrets,
# service passwords, or SSH arguments. Use the sanitized files in config/.
**/globals.yml
**/globals.yml.*
**/multinode
**/multinode.bak
**/multinode.backup
**/neutron.conf
**/neutron.conf.bak
**/neutron.conf.backup
**/ml2_conf.ini
**/ml2_conf.ini.bak
**/ml2_conf.ini.backup

# Full Kolla config copies and service-generated state must not be published.
**/etc/kolla/
**/kolla-config-backup/
**/kolla-backup/
**/kolla-logs/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 03. Private keys, signing materials, and certificates with private key data
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/id_rsa
**/id_dsa
**/id_ecdsa
**/id_ed25519
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/*.kdbx
**/*.asc

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 04. Environment variables and local credential stores
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Preserve .env.example and similarly named documentation templates.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/secrets.env
**/*.secret.env
**/.netrc
**/.pypirc
**/.python_history
**/.bash_history
**/.zsh_history

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 05. Python, Kolla Ansible, and CLI virtual environments / generated files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/env/
**/kolla-venv/
**/openstack-cli-venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.tox/
**/.nox/
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov/
**/pip-wheel-metadata/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 06. Ansible and Kolla runtime artifacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.ansible/
**/*.retry
**/ansible.log
**/ansible.cfg.local
**/facts_cache/
**/fact_cache/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 07. Logs, diagnostic dumps, and temporary output
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs can contain token values, bearer URLs, service credentials, etc.
**/*.log
**/*.log.*
**/*.trace
**/*.stackdump
**/core
**/core.*
**/*.pid
**/*.pid.lock
**/logs/
**/tmp/
**/temp/
**/.cache/
**/cache/

# Do not commit raw shell outputs unless reviewed and intentionally documented.
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
**/*.orig
**/*.rej
**/*.bak
**/*.backup

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 08. VM / image / disk artifacts — use Glance or external storage instead
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/*.qcow2
**/*.qcow
**/*.vmdk
**/*.vdi
**/*.vhd
**/*.vhdx
**/*.vma
**/*.ova
**/*.iso
**/*.img
**/*.raw
**/*.vfd

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 09. Local editor / operating-system state
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/Desktop.ini
**/$RECYCLE.BIN/
**/.Spotlight-V100/
**/.Trashes/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. Temporary build artifacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/build/
**/dist/
**/.output/
**/.tmp/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 11. Public project files: keep these trackable
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Intentionally NOT ignored (check and redact before committing):
#   README.md
#   docs/*.md
#   config/multinode.example
#   config/globals.example.yml
#   config/neutron/neutron.conf.example
#   config/neutron/ml2_conf.ini.example
#   evidence/**/*.png
#   scripts/verify-deployment.sh
#
# Do not add blanket rules like `*.png`, `*.md`, `*.yml`, `config/`, or
# `evidence/`; they would hide the project's intended documentation/evidence.
# =============================================================================
# END
# =============================================================================
